# Soren Project Rule

## Project Intent

Soren is a local-first desktop agent framework for automating browser tasks through vision-based interaction inside isolated macOS VMs.
The core loop is: assess backlog -> discover (if empty) -> execute one task -> verify/finalize -> persist results.

## Technology and Runtime

- Python `3.12+` with `uv` and `src` layout
- CLI implemented with Click (`soren` entry point)
- Core storage in SQLite (task backlog, memory, cycle reports)
- Local model stack: Ollama + UI-TARS/Qwen vision models
- VM orchestration via Lume and CUA computer tooling

## Canonical Commands

Use `justfile` commands first:

- `just begin-soren-cycle` for full orchestrated cycle
- `just refresh-tasks` for discovery-only backlog refresh
- `just list-tasks` and `just show-history` for operational visibility
- `just test` for test suite, `just lint` and `just format` for quality checks

## Architecture Guardrails

When changing code, preserve these boundaries:

- `src/soren/cli.py`: command wiring and user-facing CLI only
- `src/soren/services/meta_agent.py`: lifecycle orchestration and decision flow
- `src/soren/services/task_discovery.py`: source scanning and discovered task creation
- `src/soren/services/task_executor.py`: ComputerAgent execution, step budget, screenshots
- `src/soren/services/task_backlog.py` and `database.py`: persistence and retry lifecycle
- `src/soren/models/`: Pydantic models and schema contracts
- `src/soren/adapters/`: service-specific discovery instruction logic (not DOM scraping)

## Implementation Conventions

- Keep discovery and execution decoupled (do not merge into one inline flow).
- Prefer additive service modules over expanding CLI handlers with business logic.
- Maintain retry semantics and status transitions (`queued`, `in_progress`, `completed`, `dead_letter`).
- Keep local-only inference assumptions unless a requirement explicitly changes.
- Preserve persona-driven behavior and playbook write-back pathways.

## Testing Expectations

- Add or update unit tests in `tests/` for orchestration, backlog transitions, and adapter behavior.
- For execution/discovery changes, validate happy path plus failure classification and retry behavior.
- Use markers appropriately (`integration`, `e2e`) and keep default suite deterministic.

## Safety and Data Handling

- Do not log plaintext credentials.
- Preserve encrypted credential workflows and VM-isolated execution assumptions.
- Avoid changes that bypass memory/resource safeguards (for example, high-memory abort logic).

## Editing Guidance for AI Agents

- Start with `README.md`, `docs/rfc.md`, and `docs/prd.md` before major refactors.
- Follow existing naming and module patterns in `src/soren/services`.
- Keep patches focused and small; avoid broad rewrites when targeted edits suffice.
- After substantive changes, run `just lint` and relevant tests before concluding work.
